{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-11687-r4583539","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Boerewors (South African Sausage)","sourcePageId":11687,"sourceRevision":"4583539","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-19T18:01:09Z","sourceRevisionUser":"IB Muazzam","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Boerewors%20(South%20African%20Sausage)&oldid=4583539","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:24:43.580Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Difficult recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sausage","Category:Recipes using allspice","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using brandy","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using mutton","Category:South African recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"9fc1ad9e1825725968ed0e7b00bd4a824e2a8aa74ec1fd053f68bc8f1caa4d01","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Sausage recipes| Yield = 6 lb|servings=12|time=Cooking: 2 hours<br/>Resting: >26 hours|difficulty=4}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of South Africa|South Africa]] | [[Cookbook:Sausage|Sausage]]\n\nTraditionally eaten at ''braais'' or barbecues, '''boerewors''' (Afrikaans: farmer's sausage) are thick, hearty and flavoursome Afrikaner sausages, often eaten with a [[Cookbook:Corn|corn]] porridge called ''pap''.\n\nThere is no one definitive recipe for boerewors, as nearly every family has its own variation. Some other recipes use bacon and springbok meat. This version uses a sausage maker, and makes about 6 lb of sausage.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seed\n*2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]], [[Cookbook:Cube|cubed]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Mutton|mutton]], cubed\n*2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Veal|veal]], cubed\n*¼ [[Cookbook:pound|lb]] [[Cookbook:Spek|spek]], cubed\n*1½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n*¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] grated [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground [[Cookbook:Allspice|allspice]]\n*½ cup brown [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]]\n*1½ [[Cookbook:Brandy|brandy]] (optional)\n*2¼-inch wide [[Cookbook:Sausage casing|sausage casings]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Singed coriander ===\n#Place seeds into a dry [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]].\n#Put the pan over low heat and allow coriander to burn slightly.\n#Break seeds apart with a fork, or use a coffee/spice grinder to finely grind them.\n\n=== Sausage ===\n#Cut all meat and spek into cubes.\n#Mix spek and meat together thoroughly, and then coarsely [[Cookbook:Mincing|mince]] or grind it.\n#Mix in all dry spices, vinegar, and brandy with a large, two-pronged fork.\n#Place meat mixture in fridge, and let rest for 2 hours to blend the flavours together.\n#While the meat is resting, soak the sausage casings in water for the same 2 hours.\n#Fit casings over sausage maker, and fill with the meat/spice mixture. Be very careful not to over- or understuff the ''boerewors'', as doing so will ruin them. Fill in long continuous lengths; don't make links. \n#Cook sausages on a [[Cookbook:Grill|barbecue]], but do not prick to allow juices to escape as much of the flavour will escape with them. Cook until still pink and juicy inside\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* Try adding about 100 ml of regular oatmeal—this helps to bind the meat.\n* Be careful not to over-spice the mince, which will ruin the taste.\n* Be careful with adding salt; the spek contains plenty.\n* Boerewors can be stored for up to 3 weeks in the freezer.\n\n[[Category:South African recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sausage]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mutton]]\n[[Category:Recipes using allspice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brandy]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Boerewors (South African Sausage)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 tbsp coriander seed","sourceText":"1 tbsp coriander seed","amountText":"1 tbsp coriander seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 lb beef, cubed","sourceText":"2 lb beef, cubed","amountText":"2 lb beef, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 lb mutton, cubed","sourceText":"2 lb mutton, cubed","amountText":"2 lb mutton, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 lb veal, cubed","sourceText":"2 lb veal, cubed","amountText":"2 lb veal, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ lb spek, cubed","sourceText":"¼ lb spek, cubed","amountText":"¼ lb spek, cubed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1½ tbsp salt","sourceText":"1½ tbsp salt","amountText":"1½ tbsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 tsp ground black pepper","sourceText":"1 tsp ground black pepper","amountText":"1 tsp ground black pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"¼ tsp gr